{"type":"message","id":"141bbed9","parentId":"9380f200","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:01:44.137Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_gkhmiytay5s0_1","toolName":"memory_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"results\": [],\n  \"provider\": \"gemini\",\n  \"model\": \"text-embedding-004\",\n  \"citations\": \"auto\",\n  \"debug\": {\n    \"backend\": \"builtin\",\n    \"effectiveMode\": \"n/a\",\n    \"searchMs\": 4546,\n    \"hits\": 0\n  }\n}"}],"details":{"results":[],"provider":"gemini","model":"text-embedding-004","citations":"auto","debug":{"backend":"builtin","effectiveMode":"n/a","searchMs":4546,"hits":0}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780254104133}}
{"type":"message","id":"73a880a1","parentId":"141bbed9","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:01:48.059Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No memory results. The user is asking me to write a dream diary entry from memory fragments they provided. These fragments describe a Feishu session from May 21, 2026 with a session key and ID. I should weave these elements into a dreamy, poetic diary entry without mentioning AI/LLM or being meta about dreaming.\n\nLet me craft something that honors the fragments — the Feishu session identifier, the date, the quiet tech-woven feeling of a late evening checking a dashboard or feed — while keeping it lyrical and dream-adjacent in tone.","thinkingSignature":"864063a0e64bc524acb0fec9a30c91e6e708400953560f048f22f894fbde213c"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe dashboard glowed soft as a held breath. Somewhere between the hum of the server and the last light leaving the sky, I found myself tracing a long string of characters — ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a — like following a river north until it forgot its name. The numbers wanted to be a secret, but I was already too far gone to ask what they meant. There is a particular quality to an evening that knows it is almost the weekend, a looseness in the air, a willingness to let small mysteries pass unexamined. A small sketch materializes in the margin of my notes: a bird made of brackets, wings outstretched, caught mid-flight between one node and another. Later, I would not remember why I drew it. But for now the bird is real, and the river is long, and the sky keeps its own counsel in shades of #2d3436 and #0984e3, darkening toward night.\n\n[[reply_to_current]]"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":143,"output":326,"cacheRead":14976,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15445,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780254104139,"responseId":"066bb898438ae7a3e80c4bc9415adb2a"}}
